  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup pumpkin puree (strained)",
    "cooking spray",
    "2 teaspoon ground cinnamon",
    "2 teaspoon garam masala",
    "2 large egg",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "1 cup almond flour",
    "1/4 cup butter",
    "1/4 cup sugar-free pumpkin pie spice syrup (such as Torani)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven 400F. Get out a good knife to help cut the squash.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7000.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the squash in half. If needed, use a serrated knife or a sharp chef's knife.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7007.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Scrape out all of the innards (the stringy part, including the seeds), leaving only the pumpkin meat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7017.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the squash into wedges, following its natural contours.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7021.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the squash slices on a cookie sheet lined with parchment paper and spray with coconut oil. Season with cinnamon and garam masala, then flip over and repeat to season both sides.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7026.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for around 30–35 minutes, or until easily pierced with a fork. Remove, then turn the oven down to 350F.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7031.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add squash to a food processor. Personally, I like the texture that the skin adds, but feel free to remove the skin before this step. Note: If using canned pumpkin puree, make sure to thoroughly squeeze the moisture out of it with a cheesecloth before using.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7037.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process the squash until a thick paste is formed. Measure out the needed amount of squash into a bowl and add the eggs. Mix until combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7040.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the remaining ingredients. Mix together with a fork or by hand (my favorite method). Keep in mind that the mixture is very sticky.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7049.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a spoon or small ice cream scoop to form the dough into cookies. Place on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7059.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20–25 minutes or until the outsides have hardened, but the insides are still soft.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7088.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve as is or slice in half and spoon or pipe your favorite filling in between!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-pie-spice-scone-cookies/#wprm-recipe-51423-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
